{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":19,"code":"PSA","name":"Psalms","testament":"OT"},"chapter":45,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"d","content":["To the chief Musician upon Shoshannim, for the sons of Korah, Maschil, A Song of loves. "]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"PSA 45:1"},"My heart is inditing a good matter: I speak of the things which I have made touching the king: my tongue ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," the pen of a ready writer. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 45:1"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"PSA 45:2"},"Thou art fairer than the children of men: grace is poured into thy lips: therefore God hath blessed thee for ever. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 45:2"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"PSA 45:3"},"Gird thy sword upon ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["thy"]}," thigh, O ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["most"]}," mighty, with thy glory and thy majesty. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 45:3"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"PSA 45:4"},"And in thy majesty ride prosperously because of truth and meekness ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," righteousness; and thy right hand shall teach thee terrible things. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 45:4"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"PSA 45:5"},"Thine arrows ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," sharp in the heart of the king’s enemies; ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["whereby"]}," the people fall under thee. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 45:5"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"PSA 45:6"},"Thy throne, O God, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," for ever and ever: the sceptre of thy kingdom ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," a right sceptre. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 45:6"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"PSA 45:7"},"Thou lovest righteousness, and hatest wickedness: therefore God, thy God, hath anointed thee with the oil of gladness above thy fellows. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 45:7"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"PSA 45:8"},"All thy garments ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["smell"]}," of myrrh, and aloes, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and "]},"cassia, out of the ivory palaces, whereby they have made thee glad. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 45:8"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"PSA 45:9"},"Kings’ daughters ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["were"]}," among thy honourable women: upon thy right hand did stand the queen in gold of Ophir. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 45:9"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"PSA 45:10"},"Hearken, O daughter, and consider, and incline thine ear; forget also thine own people, and thy father’s house; ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 45:10"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"PSA 45:11"},"So shall the king greatly desire thy beauty: for he ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," thy Lord; and worship thou him. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 45:11"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"PSA 45:12"},"And the daughter of Tyre ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["shall be there"]}," with a gift; ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["even"]}," the rich among the people shall intreat thy favour. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 45:12"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"PSA 45:13"},"The king’s daughter ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," all glorious within: her clothing ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," of wrought gold. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 45:13"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"PSA 45:14"},"She shall be brought unto the king in raiment of needlework: the virgins her companions that follow her shall be brought unto thee. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 45:14"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"PSA 45:15"},"With gladness and rejoicing shall they be brought: they shall enter into the king’s palace. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 45:15"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"PSA 45:16"},"Instead of thy fathers shall be thy children, whom thou mayest make princes in all the earth. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 45:16"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"17","sid":"PSA 45:17"},"I will make thy name to be remembered in all generations: therefore shall the people praise thee for ever and ever. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 45:17"}]}]}
